IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `rvsa-owner`

-- Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 -- the import pathways and approvals, the circumstances in which a vehicle may be
-- imported or provided without one, and the modifications allowed, read from the deposited Rules. A module beside
-- rvsa-owner.l4; it works out the facts that module asks about the Rules ("a circumstance in the rules applies", "the rules
-- allow the change", "in a circumstance the rules set out") and calls its questions, restating none of them.
--
-- SEAT: the importer and owner, as in rvsa-owner.l4. "I want to import an older used car, a specialist or enthusiast vehicle,
-- my own car when I move here, or bring my car in for a visit. Which approval do I need, and on what conditions?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 5, compilation date 19 January 2024, includes amendments F2024L00086 (register id F2024C00112),
-- deposited at ../../../road-vehicle-standards-rules-2019/registers/source-bundle/F2019L00198.txt (retrieved 2026-10-23).
-- The Register named 19 January 2024's compilation as the one in force on 23 October 2026.
--
-- IN: ss 31, 32, 35-41 (the concessional RAV entry pathway and its eligibility criteria), 50 (provision without RAV entry),
-- 51 (modifications allowed), 146 (a concessional approval is an import approval), 147, 150-152 (non-RAV entry import
-- approvals), 159, 162, 163 (reimportation import approvals), 171 (importing without an approval: carnets, customs by-laws,
-- ADF vehicles); s 129 (SEVs Register eligibility) only as the fact "the model is on the SEVs Register".
-- Every criterion is "if the Minister [or the Secretary] is satisfied that ...": each is answered conditionally, as "eligible
-- if the Minister is satisfied", never as a grant. OUT: type approvals (Part 3 Div 2), the RAW, Model Report, AVV and testing
-- facility approvals (Part 4), component type approvals (Part 6), variation and revocation (Part 7), the transitional import
-- approvals (Div 2A), recalls, fees and charges.

§ `Road Vehicle Standards Rules 2019 -- the importer's questions`

§§ `ss 32, 35 to 41 -- a concessional RAV entry approval`

-- s 36: "Passenger Car (MA); Forward-control Passenger Vehicle (MB); Off-road Passenger Vehicle (MC); Moped - 2 wheels (LA);
-- Moped - 3 wheels (LB); Motor cycle (LC); Motor cycle and side-car (LD); Motor tricycle (LE); Light Goods Vehicle (NA)",
-- with "a relevant build date that is at least 25 years before the date of the application".
DECLARE `Vehicle category` IS ONE OF
    `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)`
    `a trailer`
    `another category (for example a bus or heavy goods vehicle)`

DECLARE `Concessional route` IS ONE OF
    -- s 36
    `an older vehicle: built at least 25 years before I apply`
    -- s 37
    `a specialist or enthusiast vehicle on the SEVs Register (or a used two- or three-wheeler), modified by a registered automotive workshop under an approved Model Report`
    -- s 38
    `a special purpose vehicle that cannot comply and still do its job, but is fit for public roads`
    -- s 39
    `my personal vehicle, owned and used overseas for 12 months before I moved to Australia permanently`
    -- s 40
    `a trailer`
    -- s 41
    `none of these: only that the Minister is satisfied it is suitable for entry on the RAV`

-- s 39(1): (a) no personal effects approval in the last 5 years; (b) the applicant (i) owns the vehicle, (ii) became its owner
-- "while living outside Australia on a permanent basis", (iii) "owned the vehicle for a continuous period of at least 12 months
-- immediately before the relevant date"; (c) "the application is made within 6 months of the relevant date"; (d) "intends to
-- live in Australia indefinitely"; (e) is old enough to hold a licence; (2) the vehicle was available to and regularly used by
-- the applicant on public roads there; (3) the applicant may remain indefinitely, has applied for citizenship, permanent
-- residence or such a visa, or holds a visa allowing an application for permanent residence. (4) "the relevant date": the date
-- of first arrival to live in Australia indefinitely (the latest, if more than one).
GIVEN `no personal-effects approval in the last 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I bought it while living permanently overseas, and still own it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months I owned it before I arrived` IS A NUMBER
      `months between my arrival and my application` IS A NUMBER
      `I regularly used it on public roads there` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I intend to live in Australia indefinitely, and my visa status meets s 39(3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am old enough to hold a licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the personal effects criterion is met` IF
        `no personal-effects approval in the last 5 years`
    AND `I bought it while living permanently overseas, and still own it`
    AND `months I owned it before I arrived` AT LEAST 12
    AND `months between my arrival and my application` AT MOST 6
    AND `I regularly used it on public roads there`
    AND `I intend to live in Australia indefinitely, and my visa status meets s 39(3)`
    AND `I am old enough to hold a licence for it`

DECLARE `My concessional approval` IS ONE OF
    `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)`
    `eligible only if the Minister is satisfied the vehicle is suitable for entry on the RAV (s 41)`
    `not eligible under the criterion I named`

@export Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional RAV entry approval, the approval that also lets me import it (ss 35 to 41, 146)?
GIVEN `route` IS A `Concessional route` @desc The criterion you rely on: an older vehicle; a specialist or enthusiast vehicle on the SEVs Register to be modified by a registered workshop; a special purpose vehicle; your personal vehicle when moving to Australia; a trailer; or only general suitability
      `category` IS A `Vehicle category` @desc The vehicle's category under the Australian Design Rules
      `years between its build date and my application` IS A NUMBER @desc For an older vehicle: how many whole years separate the date it was first assembled (or its last significant modification) and the date of your application
      `the SEV, workshop and Model Report conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a specialist or enthusiast vehicle: whether it is on the SEVs Register (or a used two- or three-wheeler), you own or will own it, you have or can access an approved Model Report for it, and you will meet the approval's conditions
      `it cannot comply and still do its job, but is fit for roads` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a special purpose vehicle: whether it does not comply with the national standards, could not do what it was designed for if it did, and still complies enough to be safe and appropriate on public roads
      `the personal effects conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For your personal vehicle: whether the conditions of s 39 are met (see the personal effects question)
      `the trailer conditions are met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a trailer: whether you have had fewer than 4 such approvals for trailers of its mass class in the last 12 months and you declare full compliance (with evidence over 4.5 tonnes), or substantial compliance the Minister accepts
GIVETH A `My concessional approval`
`Is my vehicle eligible for a concessional approval` MEANS
    CONSIDER `route`
    WHEN `an older vehicle: built at least 25 years before I apply` THEN
        IF `category` EQUALS `a passenger car, forward-control or off-road passenger vehicle, moped, motorcycle, tricycle or light goods vehicle (MA, MB, MC, LA-LE, NA)` AND `years between its build date and my application` AT LEAST 25
        THEN `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)`
        ELSE `not eligible under the criterion I named`
    WHEN `a specialist or enthusiast vehicle on the SEVs Register (or a used two- or three-wheeler), modified by a registered automotive workshop under an approved Model Report` THEN
        IF `the SEV, workshop and Model Report conditions are met` THEN `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)` ELSE `not eligible under the criterion I named`
    WHEN `a special purpose vehicle that cannot comply and still do its job, but is fit for public roads` THEN
        IF `it cannot comply and still do its job, but is fit for roads` THEN `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)` ELSE `not eligible under the criterion I named`
    WHEN `my personal vehicle, owned and used overseas for 12 months before I moved to Australia permanently` THEN
        IF `the personal effects conditions are met` THEN `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)` ELSE `not eligible under the criterion I named`
    WHEN `a trailer` THEN
        IF `category` EQUALS `a trailer` AND `the trailer conditions are met` THEN `eligible: the Minister may grant a concessional RAV entry approval if satisfied of the criterion; the approval is also my import approval (ss 35, 146)` ELSE `not eligible under the criterion I named`
    WHEN `none of these: only that the Minister is satisfied it is suitable for entry on the RAV` THEN
        `eligible only if the Minister is satisfied the vehicle is suitable for entry on the RAV (s 41)`

@export I am moving to Australia with my own car. Do I meet the personal effects criterion (s 39)?
GIVEN `no personal-effects approval in the last 5 years` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have not been granted a personal effects concessional approval (or a reg 13 import approval under the old Regulations) in the last 5 years
      `I bought it while living permanently overseas, and still own it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you became the owner while living outside Australia on a permanent basis, and still own it when you apply
      `months I owned it before I arrived` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months in a row you owned it immediately before you first arrived to live in Australia indefinitely
      `months between my arrival and my application` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months after that arrival you are applying
      `I regularly used it on public roads there` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, while you owned it, it was available to you and regularly used by you (or mostly by you, the rest by people you authorised) on public roads in the country you lived in
      `I intend to live in Australia indefinitely, and my visa status meets s 39(3)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you intend to live in Australia indefinitely and you may remain indefinitely, have applied for citizenship, permanent residence or a permanent visa, or hold a visa that lets you apply for permanent residence
      `I am old enough to hold a licence for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are old enough to hold a licence to drive it, in Australia or in the country you used it in
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Do I meet the personal effects criterion` IF
    `the personal effects criterion is met` `no personal-effects approval in the last 5 years` `I bought it while living permanently overseas, and still own it` `months I owned it before I arrived` `months between my arrival and my application` `I regularly used it on public roads there` `I intend to live in Australia indefinitely, and my visa status meets s 39(3)` `I am old enough to hold a licence for it`

§§ `ss 147 to 152, 159 to 163 -- other import approvals`

DECLARE `Why I am importing it` IS ONE OF
    `to drive it on public roads in Australia`
    `only for a race or rally, an exhibition of a vehicle not generally available here, filming, testing or market evaluation, or as a hot rod or other significantly modified vehicle, not generally on public roads`
    `for a temporary stay, not to be used on public roads except in exceptional circumstances`
    `to bring back my vehicle that is on the RAV (or has an identification plate) and is now outside Australia`

DECLARE `My import approval` IS ONE OF
    `a concessional RAV entry approval (s 146), or a type approval holder's authority: see the concessional approval question`
    `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied; it may require me to export or destroy it, and limit its use (ss 150, 151, 157)`
    `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied it will stay temporarily and stay off public roads; it may require me to export it (ss 150, 152, 157)`
    `a reimportation import approval, if the Secretary is satisfied that I own it and it still matches its RAV entry or plate (ss 162, 163)`

@export Which import approval do I need for the reason I am importing this vehicle (ss 146, 150 to 152, 162, 163)?
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why I am importing it` @desc Why you are importing the vehicle: to use it on Australian roads; for racing, exhibition, filming, testing or as a hot rod, not on public roads; for a temporary stay; or to bring back your own RAV-registered vehicle
GIVETH A `My import approval`
`Which import approval do I need` MEANS
    CONSIDER `why`
    WHEN `to drive it on public roads in Australia` THEN `a concessional RAV entry approval (s 146), or a type approval holder's authority: see the concessional approval question`
    WHEN `only for a race or rally, an exhibition of a vehicle not generally available here, filming, testing or market evaluation, or as a hot rod or other significantly modified vehicle, not generally on public roads` THEN `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied; it may require me to export or destroy it, and limit its use (ss 150, 151, 157)`
    WHEN `for a temporary stay, not to be used on public roads except in exceptional circumstances` THEN `a non-RAV entry import approval, if the Minister is satisfied it will stay temporarily and stay off public roads; it may require me to export it (ss 150, 152, 157)`
    WHEN `to bring back my vehicle that is on the RAV (or has an identification plate) and is now outside Australia` THEN `a reimportation import approval, if the Secretary is satisfied that I own it and it still matches its RAV entry or plate (ss 162, 163)`

§§ `ss 50, 171 -- importing or providing it with no approval`

-- s 171(1): "For the purposes of paragraph 22(2)(d) of the Act, a person is permitted to import a road vehicle if, at the time
-- of the importation, subsection (2), (3), (4), (5) or (6) applies": (2) a CPD carnet and temporary admission under Art 2(1) of
-- the Private Road Vehicles Convention; (3) an ATA carnet under the Istanbul Convention; (4) an A.T.A. carnet under the ATA
-- Convention; (5) Schedule 4 items 10 (visiting forces), 11 or 15(d) to the Customs Tariff Act applying by by-law; (6) an
-- ADF vehicle returning after an activity abroad. s 50(2)-(5): the same carnets and by-laws let the vehicle be provided
-- without RAV entry, if providing it would not break a condition of the Convention; (6): provision the Rules or an approval's
-- condition permit or require.
DECLARE `How it comes in` IS ONE OF
    `on a CPD carnet, with temporary admission under the Private Road Vehicles Convention`
    `on an ATA carnet under the Istanbul or ATA Convention`
    `under a customs by-law for Schedule 4 items 10, 11 or 15(d) of the Customs Tariff Act (for example visiting forces)`
    `as an Australian Defence Force vehicle returning from an activity abroad`
    `none of these`

GIVEN `how` IS A `How it comes in`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 171 circumstance applies` IF (NOT (`how` EQUALS `none of these`))

@export Am I permitted to import this vehicle, once the Rules' approvals and circumstances are applied (s 22, Rules ss 146, 171)?
GIVEN `it is a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a road vehicle under s 6
      `I hold a type approval for its type` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a road vehicle type approval in force for the vehicle's type
      `a type approval holder has authorised me in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the holder of a type approval in force for its type has authorised you in writing to import it
      `I hold a concessional, non-RAV entry or reimportation approval for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, when it is imported, you hold a concessional RAV entry approval, a non-RAV entry import approval or a reimportation import approval that is in force and covers this vehicle
      `how` IS A `How it comes in` @desc Whether the vehicle comes in on a CPD or ATA carnet, under a Schedule 4 customs by-law, or as a returning ADF vehicle
GIVETH A `May I import it`
`May I import this vehicle under the Rules` MEANS
    `May I import this vehicle` `it is a road vehicle` `I hold a type approval for its type` `a type approval holder has authorised me in writing` `I hold a concessional, non-RAV entry or reimportation approval for it` (`a s 171 circumstance applies` `how`)

@export I want to hand over (sell, lend, give) a vehicle that is not on the RAV. Do the Rules' circumstances let me (s 24, Rules s 50)?
GIVEN `it is a road vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is a road vehicle under s 6
      `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is entered on the RAV
      `it has been provided to someone in Australia before` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has already been sold, given, lent, leased or hired to someone in Australia
      `how` IS A `How it comes in` @desc Whether it came in on a CPD or ATA carnet, or under a Schedule 4 customs by-law (an ADF vehicle is not a s 50 case)
      `handing it over keeps to the carnet's or by-law's conditions` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether handing it over would not break a condition of the Convention or by-law it came in under (for example a ban on hire or reward)
      `the Rules or an approval's condition permit this handover` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Rules, or a condition of an approval under them, expressly or impliedly permit or require this handover (for example to a registered workshop under a concessional approval)
      `I hold a non-RAV entry import approval for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a non-RAV entry import approval that relates to it
      `it is made in Australia and I say it is not for road use` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was made in Australia and you make clear it is not for public roads, or only in exceptional circumstances
GIVETH A `May I provide it`
`May I provide this vehicle under the Rules` MEANS
    `May I provide this vehicle` `it is a road vehicle` `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` `it has been provided to someone in Australia before` `the reason` `I hold a non-RAV entry import approval for it` `it is made in Australia and I say it is not for road use`
    WHERE
        `a s 50 circumstance applies` MEANS
                `the Rules or an approval's condition permit this handover`
            OR  (    (NOT (`how` EQUALS `none of these`))
                 AND (NOT (`how` EQUALS `as an Australian Defence Force vehicle returning from an activity abroad`))
                 AND `handing it over keeps to the carnet's or by-law's conditions`)
        `the reason` MEANS
            IF `a s 50 circumstance applies` THEN `in a circumstance the rules set out` ELSE `to sell, give, lend, lease or hire it, or give access to it`

§§ `s 51 -- modifications the Rules allow`

-- s 51: allowed are modifications (a) to a type-approval-pathway vehicle to seek a type approval or a Model Report for them;
-- (b) in second stage of manufacture under a type approval's supporting information; (c) to a type-approval-pathway vehicle in
-- second stage of manufacture under an approved Model Report; (d) under the National Code of Practice Heavy Vehicle
-- Modifications as in force where modified; (e) to a type-approval-pathway vehicle, not covered by the supporting information,
-- "in accordance with written instructions provided by the holder of that approval".
DECLARE `The modification` IS ONE OF
    `to seek a type approval or a Model Report approval for it (type approval pathway vehicle)`
    `in second stage of manufacture, under the type approval's supporting information or an approved Model Report`
    `under the National Code of Practice Heavy Vehicle Modifications`
    `on the type approval holder's written instructions (type approval pathway vehicle)`
    `another modification`

@export May I modify this vehicle on the RAV before it is first provided to a consumer, once the Rules' allowed modifications are applied (s 26, Rules s 51)?
GIVEN `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the vehicle is entered on the RAV
      `it has already been provided to a consumer in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it has already been provided to a consumer in Australia for the first time
      `the change takes it outside its RAV entry pathway` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the modification would make it no longer meet the requirements of the entry pathway it was entered under
      `the modification` IS A `The modification` @desc What kind of modification it is
GIVETH A `May I modify it`
`May I modify this vehicle under the Rules` MEANS
    `May I modify this vehicle` `it is on the Register of Approved Vehicles` `it has already been provided to a consumer in Australia` `the change takes it outside its RAV entry pathway` (NOT (`the modification` EQUALS `another modification`))

§§ `Conditions, as rules`

DECLARE `RVS party` IS ONE OF
    `I, the approval holder`

DECLARE `RVS act` IS ONE OF
    `give the requested information or documents`
    `let an inspector inspect the vehicle`
    `export or destroy the vehicle`

-- s 157(1)(b): a non-RAV entry import approval is subject to "the condition that the holder of the approval must, if requested
-- in writing by the Minister or an inspector, allow or arrange for the Minister or an inspector to inspect the vehicle";
-- (2)(a): conditions may "require the holder of the approval to export or destroy the vehicle ... within a specified period".
-- Breach of a condition may be an offence or civil penalty (ss 28, 29 of the Act). The period is the approval's own.
GIVEN `the period the approval specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RVS party` `RVS act`
`the export-or-destroy condition` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the approval holder`
    MUST  `export or destroy the vehicle`
    WITHIN `the period the approval specifies`
    LEST  BREACH BY `I, the approval holder` BECAUSE "s 157(2)(a): the vehicle was not exported or destroyed in the period the non-RAV entry import approval specified (an offence or civil penalty, Act ss 28, 29)"

-- s 158: "It is a condition of a non-RAV entry import approval that the holder of the approval, when requested in writing by the
-- Minister or an inspector and within such reasonable time as is specified in the request" gives the information or documents.
GIVEN `the time the request specifies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `RVS party` `RVS act`
`the information condition` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the approval holder`
    MUST  `give the requested information or documents`
    WITHIN `the time the request specifies`
    LEST  BREACH BY `I, the approval holder` BECAUSE "s 158: requested information not given within the time the request specified"
